            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Latin for to set about, then the Latin for to foresee."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: mātūrō, mātūrāre",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "mātūrō, mātūrāre — \"to hasten; to ripen\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Iter mātūrāvit. He hurried on his journey."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "mātūrō, mātūrāre, mātūrāvī, mātūrātum, built on mātūrus, ripe, early: to bring on early. English mature."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "mātūrō is built on mātūrus \"ripe, early, timely\" (EtymDB; Lewis & Short). English mature comes from the adjective."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
